    "join_rules": [
      "Rebrickable elements.csv lists an element of the part in the color; the element ID is the lowest numeric element whose design_id equals the part number (else the lowest listed).",
      "Rebrickable colors.csv gives the Rebrickable name, id and RGB; transparent colors are excluded.",
      "LDraw LDConfig.ldr gives the LEGO name and id: the LDraw CODE equals the Rebrickable id, the names agree (case-insensitive, '_' as space, grey as gray) and a LEGOID comment precedes it.",
      "The BrickLink color guide lists a color with exactly the Rebrickable name; its id is used.",
      "Kit colors are copied from kit_colors.json, the authority for them."
    ],
    "part_numbers": {
      "6141": "Rebrickable elements.csv files element 614101 (and every other 1x1 round plate element) under part_num 6141 with design_id 6141; it lists no elements under 4073. 4073 is the BrickLink catalog number recorded in feature 003 from Brickset; no pinned BrickLink part page was checked.",
      "98138": "Rebrickable elements.csv files the 1x1 round tile under part_num 98138 (design_id 35381 for newer elements)."
    },
    "license_note": "Rebrickable's terms for its CSV downloads could not be confirmed (open question in specs/004-map-recipes/run-state.md). This file records facts (which colors a part is made in, and catalog IDs) with citations; it does not redistribute the downloads.",
